  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Senior Executive Seminar 01-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This seminar will take place a year after the international climate change summit in Glasgow, which frames this global phenomenon in the broadest sense of human security. Agriculture, energy, transportation, and security are all affected by increasingly erratic weather patterns. Earlier commitments to mitigate and address these have been uneven, and now ever-stringent requirements are being placed on countries. This course will examine such trends an provide an opportunity to compare and contrast how countries in the NESA region are responding to climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
